            {
              "title": "Director of Engineering, Security Platform",
              "caption": "Oct 2023 - Present · 2 yrs 3 mos",
              "metadata": "Los Angeles Metropolitan Area",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "- Accountable for strategic direction, design, implementation, and maintenance of software controls that manage risks inherent to Yelp’s infrastructure, assets, data, and business.\n- Lead and support 3 teams: Infrastructure Security, Identity, and Incident Detection & Response.\n- Own, automate, and evolve the continued performance of software controls across cloud security, data security, identity management, and detection engineering.\n- Empower the team to propose their own initiatives by defining annual strategic themes for the Security org.\n- Introduced project milestones emphasizing context sharing and outward communication of achievements:\n- Lead high severity incident response activities; coach direct reports in leading lower severity incidents. \n- Partner with leaders across and outside of engineering staff - including Internal Audit, GRC, Infrastructure, ML, external vendors, and more - to both understand their goals and to achieve shared goals.\n- Define agenda and lead monthly Security Steering Committee meetings with CTO and multiple VP stakeholders."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Head of Security Platform",
              "caption": "Apr 2021 - Sep 2023 · 2 yrs 5 mos",
              "metadata": "San Francisco Bay Area",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Lead a security engineering organization comprised of ~22 engineers across 3 teams that is responsible for IAM, data and cloud security, vulnerability management, and incident response. Prioritize opportunities that concurrently improve security posture, enhance developer productivity, and support growth of the wider business."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Engineering Manager, Infrastructure Security",
              "caption": "Jan 2019 - Apr 2021 · 2 yrs 3 mos",
              "metadata": "San Francisco Bay Area",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "- Accountable for transforming and improving security posture across data security, cloud security, intrusion detection, and vulnerability management.\n- Led a team of 10 engineers. Delivered regular feedback and career guidance.\n- Partnered and built relationships with leaders across SRE, ML, Audit, and more to materially improve security posture. Worked to gain context and carefully understand their goals and pain points. Translated knowledge into multiple successful cross-team collaborations.\n- Key team technical accomplishments:\n-- SSH+sudo least privilege access controls supporting 5,000 servers, backed by AD and OPA.\n-- AWS authentication for 1,250 humans, using Okta federation and JWT.\n-- Migrated Yelp’s SIEM from ElasticSearch to Splunk, saving $250,000 per year.\n-- Implemented a rule-based data retention framework to expire SI/PII according to business need.\n-- Designed a custom package analyzer in response to public typosquatting attacks.\n- Key team process accomplishments:\n-- Guided the writing of Yelp’s Data Security Policy and integrated it into the formal review process.\n-- Oversaw the migration of incident response playbooks from an ad hoc process to a SlackOps model.\n-- Launched a recurring Threat Hunting program; later, the team extended it to an org-wide process.\n-- Transitioned from informal threat modeling to a repeatable process that can be performed by any engineer outside of Security - now a required component of design review.\n-- Added vulnerability notifications to individual teams’ health status metrics."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Lead Software Engineer, Metrics Infrastructure",
              "caption": "Oct 2015 - Jan 2019 · 3 yrs 3 mos",
              "metadata": "San Francisco, CA",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "- Architected and maintained a Splunk cluster containing over 1PB storage and 35TB daily ingestion.\n- Combined 4 legacy Splunk clusters, saving $500,000 each year, without downtime or alerting gaps. \n- Deployed real-time company health monitoring for the executive team by instrumenting ~30 critical flows.\n- Trialed 2-3 new metrics vendors per year. Regularly right-sized data in existing vendors.\n- Justified and drove adoption of AWS Glacier; built the tooling and process, saving Yelp ~$2.5MM in year 1.\n- Designed a fault-tolerant time series pipeline to enable low friction application measurement."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Software Engineer, Infrastructure",
              "caption": "Jul 2013 - Oct 2015 · 2 yrs 3 mos",
              "metadata": "San Francisco Bay Area",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "- Designed and implemented a system to rotate thousands of AWS IAM credentials. Deprecated hundreds of static keys, such that AWS service keypairs are guaranteed to change several times a week. Substantially lowered the risk of long-lived credential exfiltration.\n- Designed and implemented a TB-scale performance profiling aggregator using Elastic MapReduce. Vastly simplified the process of collecting and searching profiling data from Yelp’s service stack.\n- Added canary deployment to the architecture supporting Yelp’s primary monolithic codebase.\n- Built a monitoring app to track code/config versions across hundreds of services."
                }
